      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/baseline-samples/17592186096700/assets/c0260c2bc67fee7ad2c8c8585c951f9e4b2873a2d449f2b8405c1ca8e5e9ed30.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $e$ and $c$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $e$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $e\\ne -2c$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $a$ and $b$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $a$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $a=-b$.\n\n- Statement III is true. The vectors $e$ and $c$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $e$ is $2$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $e=2c$.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true.",
