      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $d$ and $a$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $d$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $a$. So, $d\\ne -2a$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $e$ and $c$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $e$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $c$. So, $e=-c$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $d$ and $a$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $d$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $a$. So, $d\\ne 2a$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true.",
