    "question": {
      ":question/id": "27dc2b64-5468-5eb5-9036-6398deaa7748",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/baseline-samples/17592186096700/assets/a1ea957facae065be709aa33bbe34f9a42915f97bfec84113f1fa7fced83483c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram that is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- Statement I is false. The vectors $d$ and $e$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $d$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $d\\ne -2e$.\n\n- Statement II is true. The vectors $c$ and $b$ are parallel and have opposite directions. The magnitude of $c$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $b$. So, $c=-b$.\n\n- Statement III is false. The vectors $d$ and $e$ are parallel and have the same direction. The magnitude of $d$ is $1$ times the magnitude of $e$. So, $d\\ne 2e$.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
